2. Information We Collect
When you use Sift Mates, we may collect and process the following categories of information.
2.1. Information Received Through Facebook
When you access Sift Mates through Facebook Instant Games, we may receive certain information made available through Facebook’s gaming platform and the permissions granted by you.
This may include:
* Facebook Instant Games player identifier or game-scoped player ID.
* Player display name.
* Profile picture or profile image URL, where available.
* Language or locale preferences.
* Information necessary to authenticate your gameplay session.
* Other information made available through the platform’s supported APIs and permissions.
We use this information primarily to identify players, personalize the gaming experience, and enable multiplayer functionality.
We do not request your Facebook password.
2.2. Game and Gameplay Information
To provide multiplayer functionality and maintain your game progress, we collect and store information generated through your use of Sift Mates.
This may include:
* Player identifiers.
* Game IDs and match information.
* Selected game categories.
* Secret puzzles selected by players.
* Questions asked during a match.
* Answers provided by opponents.
* Final guesses and game outcomes.
* Match status, timestamps, and relevant gameplay events.
* Game statistics, including wins, losses, draws, and other performance information.
This information is necessary to operate the game, synchronize gameplay between players, maintain match history, and provide relevant statistics.
2.3. Technical and Diagnostic Information
We and our service providers may process certain technical information to maintain the security, reliability, and performance of our Services.
Depending on the platform and infrastructure, this may include:
* Application and server logs.
* Authentication and session information.
* Error reports and diagnostic information.
* Access timestamps.
* Technical information associated with requests to our backend services.
We use this information to troubleshoot issues, identify unauthorized activity, and improve the overall experience.
